-- title:
--   Lemma 3.2 of OpenAI's Primitive roots paper in the model — F_S^×/F_S^×6 is finite and has a subgroup B with [ε·gen 𝔄] ∈ B exactly when ε ∈ U_S⁶
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $n$-th roots of unity, with $n > 0$ and $12 \mid n$ (`IsCyclotomicExtension {n} ℚ F`), and let $\iota : F \to \mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism. There is $N_0$ such that for every nonzero ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $\mathcal O_F$ divisible by every nonzero prime ideal of norm at most $N_0$ (`SmallPrimesDvd N₀ 𝔪`) and every system of allowed generators $g$ (`AllowedGen ι 𝔪`) there is $k_0$ such that for every level $k \ge k_0$:
--   - `SFinCls 𝔪 k` (the bundle `Def_ArtinHeckeSModel`) is finite;
--   - there is a subgroup $B$ of `SFinCls 𝔪 k` such that for every exterior ideal $\mathfrak A$ and every $S$-unit $\varepsilon$ (`SUnit 𝔪`), the class of the finite part of `sEmb 𝔪 k` $(\varepsilon\cdot g.\mathrm{gen}\,\mathfrak A)$ lies in $B$ if and only if $\varepsilon$ is a sixth power in `SUnit 𝔪`.
--
--   This is a cut for `exists_cutoff_exists_mellin_thetaAverage_eq_tsum_localWhittaker`, used with `exists_cutoff_exists_tsum_thetaWhittaker_sub_tsum_weylWhittaker_radial` and `exists_cutoff_exists_sChar_sEmb_gen_eq_thetaChar_mul_residueSymbol`; that reduction is proved in Lean. $B$ selects, among the frequencies $\varepsilon A$ ($A$ an allowed generator), those with $\varepsilon \in U_S^6$, as the indicator $\mathbf 1_B([y])$ does in the forward unfolding of the paper (p. 30).
--
--   In the paper this is Lemma 3.2 (p. 10): $U_S/U_S^6 \to \mathcal V = F_S^\times/F_S^{\times6}$ is injective with image $E$, and $\mathcal V = E \oplus B$ with the classes of the allowed generators in $B$. Here the generators are those of an arbitrary `AllowedGen`, so $B$ is the complement generated by their classes.
--
--   OpenAI, *Primitive roots for every admissible integer base* (2026), p. 10: “The pairing $H_S$ on $\mathcal V$ is nondegenerate and alternating. The map $U_S/U_S^6 \to \mathcal V$ is injective, its image $E$ satisfies $E^\perp = E$, and there is an isotropic subgroup $B$ such that $\mathcal V = E \oplus B$.”
--
--   **Formalization note.** $\mathcal V$ is `SFinCls 𝔪 k`, the model's finite part modulo sixth powers, for every large level $k$.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Primitive roots for every admissible integer base, OpenAI Math Release preprint, October 4, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Primitive-roots-for-every-admissible-integer-base-October-4-2026/primitive-roots-all-integer-bases.pdf (Apache-2.0), p. 9–10, Lemma 3.2 (U_S/U_S⁶ ↪ 𝒱 = F_S^×/F_S^{×6} and 𝒱 = E ⊕ B, with B generated by the classes of the allowed generators); a cut for exists_cutoff_exists_mellin_thetaAverage_eq_tsum_localWhittaker

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHecke
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHeckeProbe
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHeckeTheta
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHeckeSModel

namespace ArtinPrimitiveRoots

open NumberField UniqueFactorizationMonoid

open Classical in
theorem exists_cutoff_finite_sFinCls_and_exists_addSubgroup_mem_iff_mem_range_pow_six (n : ℕ) (hn0 : 0 < n) (hn : 12 ∣ n)
    (F : Type*) [Field F] [NumberField F] [IsCyclotomicExtension {n} ℚ F] (ι : F →+* ℂ) :
  ∃ N₀ : ℕ, ∀ 𝔪 : Ideal (𝓞 F), 𝔪 ≠ ⊥ → SmallPrimesDvd N₀ 𝔪 →
    ∀ (g : AllowedGen ι 𝔪),
    ∃ k₀ : ℕ, ∀ k : ℕ, k₀ ≤ k →
      Finite (SFinCls 𝔪 k) ∧
      ∃ B : AddSubgroup (SFinCls 𝔪 k), ∀ 𝔄 : Ideal (𝓞 F), IsExterior 𝔪 𝔄 → ∀ ε : SUnit 𝔪,
        ((QuotientAddGroup.mk (sEmb 𝔪 k ((ε : Fˣ) * (g.gen 𝔄 : F))).2.2 : SFinCls 𝔪 k) ∈ B ↔
          ε ∈ (powMonoidHom 6 : SUnit 𝔪 →* SUnit 𝔪).range)
  := by
  sorry

end ArtinPrimitiveRoots
